  "title": "Leelakittisin2025: Sit-to-stand / stand-to-sit transition motor imagery dataset",
  "description": "A BIDS re-release of an EEG dataset targeting sit-to-stand and stand-to-sit transitions during motor execution and motor imagery. It includes 22 healthy participants recorded over two sessions each with 60-channel EEG, 2 EOG channels and EMG at a 1200 Hz sampling rate. The dataset supports study of neural activation patterns and brain-computer interface decoding of lower-limb postural transitions.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was recorded at 1200 Hz from 60 scalp channels (10-05 montage), plus 2 EOG and 6 EMG channels, with trigger codes on a stim channel. Participants performed sit-to-stand and stand-to-sit transitions under motor execution and motor imagery conditions, with two rounds of 10 trials per task per session and a 4 s trial duration.",
